<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Gives sleep back when a Lid Closed Mode session reaches a configured limit.

      A lid-closed Mac on battery is usually in a bag, where it would otherwise run flat and
      can run hot. The app cannot handle this itself: restoring sleep needs root, and with
      the lid shut nobody can answer a password prompt.

      A one-shot fired every minute by StartInterval, not a persistent process: each run
      reads the root-owned session marker and system power and thermal state, then exits.
      It accepts no input from anyone, so
      it adds no IPC surface. It does nothing unless LidClosed's marker is present, and
      unlike the boot cleanup it acts while the app is running, on purpose.

      The original label and subcommand remain so an installed daemon can use an updated helper.
    -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.akwnnwastaken.LidClosed.batteryguard</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/Library/PrivilegedHelperTools/com.akwnnwastaken.LidClosed.helper</string>
        <string>battery-guard</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
